our loader does not have a real state - we want to optimize the cache life time for performance

lets say `a.tsx` and `b.tsx` have the same file `macro.ts` as dependency because we added it with `this.addDependency` 

now once `macro.ts` is changed turbopack will run the loader twice - once for `a.tsx` and once for `b.tsx`

this is correct and expected but we have to evaluate `macro.ts` twice in the same compilation although `macro.ts` can change only once per compilation

vite gives us all changed files so we destroy the cache per file before their compilation starts:

```ts
    configureServer(server) {
      server.watcher.on("change", (file) => {
        evaluator.invalidate(file);
      });
    },
```

for webpack we basically do for each `this._compilation` a full cache reset: `evaluator.invalidateAll()`

for turbopack we can't optimize at all
